module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.duplicate_declaration_arrives_through_a_clean_merge

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data duplicate_declaration_arrives_through_a_clean_merge: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "duplicate_declaration_arrives_through_a_clean_merge" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a branch appends a declaration to an append-only carrier that its OWN MERGE BASE already carries, and the three-way text merge reports nothing, because both sides are INSERTIONS AT DIFFERENT OFFSETS and text merge is offset-based rather than identity-based.** INVALID STATE: one module declares one name twice, each copy byte-identical to the other, arriving through a merge that never saw a conflict. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, MEASURED (gunbc, 2026-09-03).** `absence_classifier_default_bucket` and `green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own` were first added to `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` by gunbc#10166 (2bba578d56e) at 07:29Z. gunbc#10236 (cfe19ea7f48) added BOTH a second time at 19:49Z; its entire diff on that file is `+4` lines and nothing else. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 2bba578d56e cfe19ea7f48` holds, so the branch re-added two declarations that ALREADY EXISTED IN ITS OWN BASE. Counting additions of those two declaration lines per commit touching the file scores #10236 at 2 and #9981, #10269, #10252 and #10248 at 0 each, which is what separates the cause from the traffic around it. ",

    "**THE ROW EXISTS TO NAME THE BELIEF IT FALSIFIES, WHICH IS WRITTEN DOWN IN THE CARRIER'S OWN HEADER.** `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` says of its split into rows: \"two lanes touch two declarations and never collide, while two lanes editing the SAME class still conflict -- which is correct, because that is real disagreement about one fact\". THAT HOLDS FOR EDITS AND FAILS FOR APPENDS. An edit to an existing region is anchored to context both sides share, so a text merge sees the overlap; an append is anchored to nothing, so two appends of the SAME identity at two offsets are, to the merge, two unrelated additions. And an append is the only operation an append-only roster performs -- so the carrier's contention model was reasoned entirely about the case it does not have. ",

    "HARM, AND WHY IT ARRIVES LATE AND WIDE: a duplicate declaration is refused at RESOLVE, loudly and correctly -- `duplicate declaration <name> in module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode`, located and naming the module -- but the refusal fires when someone resolves the authority, which is after landing. On 2026-09-03 that was main, for roughly eighty minutes, and it stopped every concurrent lane that needed to regenerate a generated artifact, not the author who wrote it. ",

    "**WHY THE PROJECTION-FIDELITY GATE WAS GREEN THROUGHOUT, which is the part a reader will otherwise assume was drift.** `gunbc.design_ledgers` projects `docs/design-failure-modes.md` by mapping over the ROSTER, and the roster names each identity exactly once, so a duplicated DECLARATION renders nowhere. The projection was byte-correct, the drift gate had nothing to report, and deleting the duplicates changed no projection bytes. A check whose subject is the projection cannot see a defect in the declaration set the projection selects FROM. ",

    "DISTINCT FROM `premise_that_a_shared_subject_means_disagreement`, WHICH QUOTES THE SAME HEADER SENTENCE AND IS A DIFFERENT FINDING. That row's invalid state is a PREMISE that classified a recurring cost -- author time spent hand-negotiating byte order inside one row -- as intended, so nobody measured it. This row's invalid state is a MERGE RESULT: the same sentence also asserts that lanes touching two declarations \"never collide\", and the failure here is that two lanes appending the SAME declaration collide semantically while not colliding textually, which lands a module that cannot resolve. One sentence, one axis missed on each side: that row loses a cost, this row loses a refusal. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: for any carrier whose normal operation is APPEND, ask what the merge is comparing. If it compares LINE REGIONS, then identity collisions between two appends are invisible by construction, and the absence of a conflict is evidence about offsets and about nothing else. The tell in the record is a diff that is purely additive, mergeable without incident, and semantically a duplicate of content already above it. ",

    "DISTINCT FROM `authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded`: that row is about which merge DRIVER a path resolves to. This row holds even where the driver is correct, because a driver that merges text is still merging text -- the defect is the grain of the comparison, not its configuration. ",

    "DISTINCT FROM `append_only_carrier_whose_serialization_shares_a_merge_region`, WHICH LANDED ON MAIN WHILE THIS ROW WAS IN REVIEW AND IS THIS ROW'S EXACT DUAL. That class is a CONFLICT THAT CARRIES NO INFORMATION: two lanes append logically disjoint rows, the serialization puts them in one merge region, and the textual merge refuses a union whose answer is mechanically determined. This class is A COLLISION THAT PRODUCES NO CONFLICT: two lanes append the SAME identity, the serialization puts them at different offsets, and the textual merge accepts a result that cannot resolve. Same carrier, same merge, opposite errors -- one refuses where it should union, the other unions where it should refuse -- and neither repair is the other's. A serialization in which independent appends do not share a merge region retires that row and leaves this one exactly where it is, because the defect here is not WHERE the comparison happens but WHAT it compares: offsets rather than identities. This row was originally filed as `append_only_carrier_re_adds_what_its_own_base_already_carries` and renamed on the merge that brought the two together, because two rows opening with the same four words is the fusion DESIGN section 3 warns about. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The compiler refuses the resulting state totally and with a located diagnostic, so the ordinary floor held and no wrong answer was produced; what was unheld is everything before the refusal. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The merge of an append-only carrier is decidable at IDENTITY grain -- the declaration sets of base, ours and theirs are enumerable, and a result whose declaration set repeats an identity can be refused as a merge result rather than discovered as a compile failure later. It is not rung 4 while the carrier's contents are reached through a general-purpose text merge that can construct any byte sequence. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AS A DIAGNOSTIC THAT WOULD CONTRIBUTE TO ONE: a merge over append-only carriers that combines DECLARATION SETS rather than line regions, sufficient to REFUSE a merge result in which one identity is declared twice, with a discriminating RED (base carrying an identity, one side re-adding it at a different offset, refused) and an accepted positive control (two sides appending two distinct identities, merged additively). A parse-time or resolve-time duplicate diagnostic is a better message about the same landed state and does not discharge this trigger, because it still fires after the merge that should not have produced it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
